# fzf (this Mac)

Fuzzy finder is installed and part of the shell/dotfiles setup.

- Binary: `~/.local/bin/fzf` (dotfiles build; shadows Homebrew’s `/opt/homebrew/bin/fzf`)
- Version: ~0.74.x — also linked via Homebrew formula `fzf`
- Defaults: `FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS` already set (`--ansi`, half-height, tmux pane, top border, reverse-list)
- Related: `fzf-tmux`, zsh `fzf-tab`, helpers `fz` / `fgb` / `fgl` / `fgd` / `bag` in dotfiles
- Good companions already present: `rg`, `bat`, `fd`

## Usage for agents

Prefer `fzf` for **interactive** pick-from-list flows when a TTY/user is present (branch pick, file pick, history). Do **not** reinstall via brew/curl, and do not invent alternate fuzzy UIs when `fzf` fits.

Non-interactive agent shells (`CURSOR_AGENT`, no TTY): use `fzf -f` / `--filter` only; skip live TUI. See also `agent-shell.mdc` for env load order. `FZF_DEFAULT_OPTS` lives in `rc.d` and may be absent unless the Cursor snap restored it.
